  "questionnaireAbout": "About the scores",
  "questionnaireAboutBody": "MIDAS adds up five day counts: 0 to 5 is grade I (little or no disability), 6 to 10 grade II (mild), 11 to 20 grade III (moderate), 21 and over grade IV (severe). HIT-6 gives 6, 8, 10, 11 or 13 points per answer, 36 to 78 in all: up to 49 is little or no impact, 50 to 55 some impact, 56 to 59 substantial impact, 60 and over severe impact. The bands are the published ones; the scores are for you and your clinician to discuss.",
  "questionnaireMidasIntro": "Think about the last three months. Count days; a day counts once per question.",
  "questionnaireMidasQ1": "On how many days did you miss work or school because of your headaches?",
  "questionnaireMidasQ2": "On how many days was your productivity at work or school reduced by half or more because of your headaches? (Do not count days you missed.)",
  "questionnaireMidasQ3": "On how many days did you not do household work because of your headaches?",
  "questionnaireMidasQ4": "On how many days was your productivity in household work reduced by half or more because of your headaches? (Do not count days you did none.)",
  "questionnaireMidasQ5": "On how many days did you miss family, social or leisure activities because of your headaches?",
  "questionnaireMidasA": "On how many days did you have a headache? (If a headache lasted more than one day, count each day.)",
  "questionnaireMidasB": "On a scale of 0 to 10, on average how painful were these headaches? (0 = no pain, 10 = pain as bad as it can be)",
  "questionnaireMidasUnscored": "Not part of the score",
