  "routineStretchesTitle": "Gentle neck and shoulder stretches",
  "routineStretchesSummary": "Five slow movements to ease tightness in your neck and shoulders. Stop if anything hurts.",
  "routineStretchesSteps": "Sit tall with your shoulders relaxed and your feet flat.\nSlowly tilt your right ear towards your right shoulder. Hold for 15 seconds, then switch sides.\nLower your chin towards your chest and hold for 15 seconds.\nRoll your shoulders backwards five times, then forwards five times.\nClasp your hands behind your back and gently open your chest for 15 seconds.",
  "@routineStretchesSteps": {"description": "One step per line."},
  "routineBreathingTitle": "Paced breathing",
  "routineBreathingSummary": "Breathe in for 4 seconds and out for 6, for about a minute. A slow out-breath helps many people settle.",
  "routineBreathingSteps": "Sit or lie down somewhere comfortable.\nBreathe in through your nose while the circle grows.\nBreathe out slowly while it shrinks.\nKeep going for six rounds, or for as long as feels good.",
  "@routineBreathingSteps": {"description": "One step per line."},
  "routineLowLightTitle": "Low light and quiet",
  "routineLowLightSummary": "Bright light and noise bother many people on sensitive days and during an attack.",
  "routineLowLightSteps": "Dim the lights or close the curtains.\nTurn on dark mode and lower your screen brightness.\nWear an eye mask or sunglasses if light still bothers you.\nCut down noise with earplugs or a quiet room.",
  "@routineLowLightSteps": {"description": "One step per line."},
  "routineHydrationTitle": "Drink some water",
  "routineHydrationSummary": "Keeping water within reach makes it easier to drink through the day.",
  "routineHydrationSteps": "Keep a glass or bottle of water within reach.\nTake a few sips every hour.\nHave a glass of water with each meal.",
  "@routineHydrationSteps": {"description": "One step per line."},
  "routineCaffeineTitle": "Keep caffeine steady",
  "routineCaffeineSummary": "Big changes in how much caffeine you have can matter for some people.",
  "routineCaffeineSteps": "Have caffeine at about the same times each day.\nAvoid big increases, and avoid suddenly skipping your usual amount.\nHave your last caffeinated drink by early afternoon.",
  "@routineCaffeineSteps": {"description": "One step per line."},
  "routineSleepTitle": "Steady sleep",
  "routineSleepSummary": "A regular sleep schedule, weekends included, helps many people.",
  "routineSleepSteps": "Go to bed and get up at about the same time every day.\nKeep the bedroom dark, quiet and cool.\nPut screens away 30 minutes before bed.\nAvoid long naps late in the day.",
  "@routineSleepSteps": {"description": "One step per line."},
